Dear yayopoint,

I would like to thank you for your suggestions. Unfortunately, most of the people
contributing to RKWard (including myself) are a little busy, so don't expect
miracles.

On the plugin: The main idea in developing RKWard is to use as less libraries
as possible (memory and speed issues). This plugin N to 1 is based on table
and chisq.test functions and also contains a barplot option with sufficient
level parametrization. The vcd package will load itself and more three packages
(MASS, grid and colorspace) and will give as return the likelihood ratio,
Phi-Coefficient, Contingency Coeff. and Cramer's V. I really don't know where
is the break-even point there and how useful it would be for the users.

Kind Regards,
Ilias

